WEBVTT

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:34.800
Excuse me.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.040
Hi, Miss Nanami.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:44.760
Now's the time for you to start working on 
QUARTET NIGHT's Triple S entry song.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.140
Okay.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:51.650
As you know, the opening artist 
screening is a concert.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:58.610
Many, many great other artists 
will be performing at the same event.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.740
But Miss Nanami...

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:08.120
I want you to write a number one song 
that will make QUARTET NIGHT shine!

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:11.870
A number one song that will make them shine?

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.330
So...

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.590
You're coming on a trip with us.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.360
A trip?

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:28.810
Yes! I'm sending you on a trip to compose 
QUARTET NIGHT's entry song right now!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.400
Let's go.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.380
Th-This is too sudden!

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.530
<i>Good.</i>

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:51.120
We're staying here?

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:52.840
Yep.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:56.010
Where are the others?

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.250
Aren't we meeting them here?

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:04.220
There they are.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.970
You're late.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:11.140
You commoner. How dare you make me wait.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:16.150
I know. Don't make us wait forever 
when you're the one who invited us.

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:19.360
You're all raring to go.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:20.990
Shut up.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.800
You're the last one here.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.820
Yeah. You can leave, if you want.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.330
So mean...

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:33.160
<i>Grandmother.</i>

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:39.720
<i>Their normally cool attitudes 
feel a little different.</i>

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.510
<i>I'm sure I can compose a wonderful song.</i>

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:57.060
What? Haruka went on a trip 
to write their entry song?

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:01.070
Yeah. Rin-chan told me 
about it before I came.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:05.110
QUARTET NIGHT is finally making their move.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.280
Yeah.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:10.090
I wish we could work on our song.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:14.180
But the president hasn't contacted us yet.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:18.000
I know, but...

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:21.270
We're doing our best, right?

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:21.960
Yeah.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.180
Maybe we're still lacking something.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:35.730
Our only option is to put all 
our efforts into what we can do.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:39.400
Yes. A journey of a thousand 
leagues starts with one step.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.440
We have to keep moving forward, 
little by little.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:45.540
Yes. I want to move forward.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.540
We're ready for you, STARISH!

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:50.660
Coming!

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:52.720
Let's go.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:12.230
You're not usually so quiet, Reiji.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.060
Hey, Reiji.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.600
Are you listening?

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:23.570
When I realized this day had 
finally come, I was just so happy!

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.620
You're overexcited.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:29.300
He's right. We haven't done anything yet.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.050
Let's get started.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.320
Roger that!

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.930
So what are we going to do?

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:38.290
We're approaching the song 
differently this time, right?

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:49.430
Um... What does that mean?

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:53.680
Normally, we don't get involved in songwriting.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:54.690
What?

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:59.390
We just sing the songs 
submitted by the composer.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:03.400
Yeah. After all, I can sing anything.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.520
You're not the only one.

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:09.110
We're professionals. It's part of the job.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:15.080
But I talked to all of you 
when I wrote your solo songs.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.310
That's right. That's why we're here.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:25.210
Since it went so well, 
we thought we'd try it again.

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:26.670
Yeah.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.840
You're right.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:36.100
Let's do our best together!

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:43.560
Well...

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:50.650
Considering the screening format, 
we should do a powerful and passionate song.

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.280
You're as simplistic as ever.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:57.330
Huh? What's that mean?

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:04.040
If you want to make an impact, 
we should do a grand and magnificent song.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:08.050
Nothing's more powerful than rock.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:12.830
Nonsense. This is why we don't get along.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:14.090
What did you say?

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:17.100
The screening is a concert.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:21.730
If we want to generate excitement, 
we should do a faster song with at least 120 BPM.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:27.330
An up-tempo dance song.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.660
You're right.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:31.610
But it's difficult to balance.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:34.000
Of course.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:38.240
But the same is true 
of magnificent and rock songs.

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:47.330
Then I think we should do 
a song that makes listeners happy.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.290
Happy?

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:51.440
That's too abstract.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:54.680
We don't know how you're defining happiness.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:56.610
Happiness...

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:01.800
It exists inside the hearts 
of those who listen to our song.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:04.200
What?

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:06.470
Huh?

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.230
What do you think, kiddo?

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:11.780
What?

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:25.330
The president told me to write a number 
one song that would make you shine.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.290
A number one song...

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:29.750
...that makes us...

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:32.710
...shine?

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:37.560
Let's take a break.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:40.400
Huh?

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.190
Where are you going?

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:44.130
I'm hungry. I'm going to eat.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:50.790
You're so good with your hands.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.010
You're in the way.

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:53.650
I want some, too!

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:55.770
There's none for you.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:58.610
I'm making this because I'm hungry.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:07.460
Thanks for the food!

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.070
It's good!

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:13.260
You're right.

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:14.090
Yeah.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:18.840
It's delicious!

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:20.710
Isn't it?

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:23.120
You didn't make it.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.190
You're right.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:24.870
Yeah.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:36.690
You're in a good mood today.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:43.530
Seriously. That was finger-licking good.

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:45.580
Finger-licking good?

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:49.800
It's in my database, but I've 
never heard anyone use it before.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:53.540
That's because no one says that anymore.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:54.250
Yeah.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:57.600
What? That's not true!

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:00.130
All the young people are saying it!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:04.050
Sheesh. You guys are missing out!

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:39.080
Camus-senpai.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:47.090
There are sights you 
can't see unless you're sincere.

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:49.930
Do you see something?

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.520
We're so high up.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.410
Don't let this satisfy you.

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:10.830
I will show you even greater heights.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.620
Thank you.

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:28.270
There you are.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:28.710
What?

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:32.870
Mikaze-senpai.

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:35.190
Are you done with the song?

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:38.770
No, but I'm almost finished.

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:46.740
Since you're all singing this song, 
I wanted to combine all your personalities.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:49.530
Combine all of us?

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:50.710
Yes.

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:56.030
But we're nothing alike.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:58.210
We've always been this way.

00:12:58.730 --> 00:12:59.960
Are you sure?

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:07.970
Since the day you met, 
you've been creating beautiful harmonies.

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:10.430
Really?

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:16.490
Yes. So let's write something 
that embodies all of you.

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:20.060
That's the value of being with someone.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:20.900
Yes.

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:25.360
It doesn't look like rain tonight.

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:35.760
You're right.

00:13:53.260 --> 00:13:54.790
Kurosaki-senpai.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.560
That's a wonderful bass.

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:00.690
I've had it a long time.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:10.660
Have we changed?

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:17.430
How's the song coming along?

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:18.960
Same as usual.

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:22.960
I promise it'll be a good song.

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:24.290
Okay.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:29.260
Let's write one that 
will blend all your passions.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:38.440
Friends are people 
you share your passion with.

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:39.460
What?

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.370
Hey, kiddo.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.560
Up here.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.500
Kotobuki-senpai.

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:07.660
There.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.390
How are you doing?

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:14.650
I'm almost finished.

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:15.720
Really?

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:22.310
I can't believe they're expressing 
their own opinions. They've changed.

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:27.190
Though they're not good, by any means.

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.680
I disagree.

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:30.830
Really?

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:34.570
You're all facing forward 
with the same thoughts.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:36.360
Besides...

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:42.170
You're all still shining the way 
you were the moment you first met.

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:04.870
When we came here before, 
we told them to climb up.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.090
We told that to STARISH.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:13.290
Their growth has exceeded our expectations.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:30.220
You knew.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.960
That song was amazing.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:42.910
Yeah. Just from listening, 
I knew who would sing which parts.

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:45.160
That's not all.

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:50.170
Yeah. That song is us.

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:53.330
We're QUARTET NIGHT.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:57.880
We didn't give it much thought 
when Shining-san had us join.

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:02.750
But now we want to work together, right?

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:07.890
What do we do now?

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:09.590
Write the lyrics.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:14.230
Since we're performing at a concert, 
we should decide how we're singing it.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:16.380
Good idea.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:20.780
Then why don't we start with the chorus?

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.490
The chorus?

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:28.490
Yeah. Instead of singing separately, 
we'll all start singing together.

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:31.200
Should we try it a capella?

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:34.230
How about adding voices to a solo?

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:39.330
Then the choreography 
should start with a strong first step.

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.050
In that case...

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:44.490
Then...

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:47.010
Yeah.

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:49.570
It'll work.

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:07.850
This song's concept 
is a passion we can share.

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:14.190
A song we play because we're together.

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:21.210
With utmost sincerity, we'll show you 
an endless panorama from great heights.

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:26.150
The five of us should write it together.

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:31.350
My girl.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:37.100
QUARTET NIGHT couldn't exist without you.

00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:36.110
It's finished.

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:38.870
Yes.

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:54.190
They've been really good lately.

00:21:54.190 --> 00:21:56.760
STARISH is even better than before.

00:21:56.760 --> 00:22:00.180
STARISH isn't entering the Triple S?

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:04.900
QUARTET NIGHT's representing 
the Shining Agency, right?

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:08.210
What? Can't they both enter?

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:09.930
Yeah, I'd love to see it!

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:11.640
Me, too!

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:13.270
Wait a minute!

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:16.430
There's already a favorite, 
but everyone's talking about them!

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:17.440
Isn't it amazing?

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:20.190
They're truly popular now.

00:22:20.930 --> 00:22:24.780
But what's Shining going to do?

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:26.200
Yeah.

00:24:06.720 --> 00:24:08.530
Thanks for your continued support.

00:24:08.530 --> 00:24:10.020
I love you all.

00:24:10.020 --> 00:24:11.220
Uta Pri.
